I've now managed to reproduce this bug in wizard mode.  You don't 
need any intrinsics to get "telepathy" into one room.

Here's how to reproduce it:

1. Find a room with a door right next to the corner:

  ------
 #-@..F| (Note: I used ^g to create a monster in the room)
  |....|
  |....|
  -+----

2. Dig out the corner:

  .-----
 #-@..F|
  |....|
  |....|
  -+----

3. Walk to the corner:

  @-----
 #-...F|
  |....|
  |....|
  -+----

4. Walk out, and you can still see in:

  #-----
 @-...F|
  |....|
  |....|
  -+----

The trick is, when you are standing on the corner of a room, and
move diagonally to get out, nethack doesn't seem to detect that 
you've left the room.  Once you enter another lit room, nethack
detects it and the effect ends.  I haven't yet looked in the source
to see why this happens.

